%% DOCURA - Diagram 16 - Document Status State Machine
%% The five statuses are exactly those named in FR-UPL-005; no status is invented here.
%% Superseded and Deleted are derived from FR-DOC-005/006 and FR-DOC-007/008.
%% Derived from: FR-UPL-005, FR-OCR-006/009/010, FR-INF-003/005, FR-DOC-005/007/008, EC-001 to EC-004
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Validating : USER selects a file

    Validating --> Rejected : unsupported, oversized, or corrupt
    Validating --> Queued : accepted
    Rejected --> [*] : never enters the vault

    Queued --> Queued : interrupted upload retried
    Queued --> Processing : picked up asynchronously

    Processing --> Failed : EC-001 extraction fails
    Processing --> NeedsReview : EC-002 value below threshold
    Processing --> NeedsReview : EC-003 type undetermined
    Processing --> NeedsReview : EC-004 documents disagree
    Processing --> Ready : classified and extracted

    Failed --> Processing : USER retries
    Failed --> Ready : USER enters it manually
    Failed : ORIGINAL ALWAYS RETAINED.
    Failed : Still stored and searchable by label.

    NeedsReview --> Ready : USER corrects or resolves
    NeedsReview : Below-threshold values NEVER
    NeedsReview : fill automatically — BR-002.
    NeedsReview : A conflict leaves NEITHER
    NeedsReview : value authoritative — BR-004.

    Ready --> NeedsReview : a new document introduces a conflict
    Ready --> Processing : USER requests reprocessing
    Ready : User corrections survive
    Ready : reprocessing — BR-012.
    Ready : The original is never
    Ready : modified — BR-013.

    Ready --> Superseded : USER adds a newer version
    Superseded --> Ready : USER designates it primary
    Superseded : The previous version is
    Superseded : RETAINED, not discarded.

    Ready --> Deleted : USER deletes, after confirmation
    Superseded --> Deleted : USER deletes
    Deleted --> Ready : restored within the grace period
    Deleted --> [*] : grace elapses — file, information<br/>and derived copies destroyed
